GfxLookUp interrupt regression
=============================

Run gfxlookup on native Amiga AROS after a normal DOS boot. The program
associates a ViewExtra, holds the graphics hash semaphore in its task, and
looks up present and absent associations from a VBlank interrupt. It also
checks task-context lookup and removal of the association.

Expected: GFX LOOKUP TEST: 0 failures, return code 0, and no supervisor-mode
semaphore diagnostic or alert. The previous implementation emits both
ObtainSemaphoreShared and ReleaseSemaphore supervisor-mode diagnostics;
the resulting alert is delivered asynchronously, so its return code alone
is not sufficient to determine success.
